stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Fenced - Modes A and B only, no submit action" as Fenced
    state "Counsel cleared for this portal and filing type" as Counsel
    state "Authority to act executed for this registration" as Instrument
    state "Mode C enabled - operator may submit" as ModeC
    state "Suspended - submit actions withdrawn at once" as Suspended

    [*] --> Fenced
    Fenced --> Counsel: Opinions recorded for CR-17a to CR-17f, scoped to this surface
    Counsel --> Instrument: Customer executes the instrument covering this registration
    Instrument --> ModeC: Liability clause in the contract and insurance position recorded
    ModeC --> Suspended: Portal terms change, opinion reopened, instrument revoked, or re-verification lapses
    Suspended --> ModeC: Cause cleared and all four gates re-verified
    Suspended --> Fenced: CR-17a or CR-17b answered adversely for this portal
    ModeC --> Fenced: CR-17a or CR-17b answered adversely for this portal

    note right of Fenced
        One row per tenant, registration, portal and filing type.
        A 90-person tenant with EPF, ESIC, TAN and PT in three states
        holds six rows and thirty-six counsel cells.
    end note

    note right of ModeC
        Mode is derived, never chosen by the operator.
        Per-filing approval is always required.
        Payment initiation stays the customer's act by default.
        A Mode D session on our credentials is a Mode C session here.
    end note
